Subject: [PATCH] hip : allow host constexpr use of the physical warp size

Clang 24 (ROCm 10.1) rejects a reference to a __device__ function in a
host constant initializer, e.g. the scrambled tile's "ne" member in
mma.cuh. The value only depends on target macros, so drop the __device__
qualifier; constexpr functions are implicitly host and device.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/common.cuh b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/common.cuh
index 928607c..dfbb489 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/common.cuh
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/common.cuh
@@ -387,7 +387,7 @@ static bool ggml_cuda_is_aligned(const ggml_tensor * tensor, const size_t alignm
            tensor->nb[3] % alignment == 0;
 }
 
-static constexpr __device__ int ggml_cuda_get_physical_warp_size() {
+static constexpr int ggml_cuda_get_physical_warp_size() {
 #if defined(GGML_USE_HIP) && (defined(__GFX9__) || defined(__GFX8__))
     return 64;
 #else
